				<td width="100%" class="title" colspan="2">I sent out this letter to all...</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3597">Kaledine</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">2/8/2002 - 4:26 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2879">Kaledine Ursamaje</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2917">Karuune Bogglesworth</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2918">Dambae Meadowlark</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														...however, I don't have everyone's email address, so I wanted to give everyone a chance to see it.  So, here goes...<br />
<br />
<br />
I'm so sorry for not sending this out sooner, but in the past month, since I've stopped playing EQ, I've had limited time available to me to do anything online, and having a very certain priority, I have not been able to get my address book in order until now.  <br />
<br />
First, I would like to explain why I disappeared so suddenly.  As many of you know, I was always on the game, and towards the end, when I wasn't on as much, it was because I was on DAoC or just surfing.  In essence, I spent about 10 hours a day on the computer, at least, if not more.  I did go to work, performed well, etc., but I didn't even have time for my sister when she came into town, as I was too caught up in the game to go out with her or sit and chat with her for a few hours.  I never spent time with my family or friends, and eventually wound up hurting those close to me.  In short, I have gotten rid of my DSL connection, resorting to (ugh) dial-up on AOL, and heading for Tryuna's if I feel the need to play EQ, which is a half hour away, so I don't have the convenience of playing right at my fingertips.  I am leaving in less than 30 days for basic training [in the Air Force], and need to get my life in order before leaving, and my constant online life wasn't allowing for that.  So, with lots of help from my parents, I have gotten EQ and the internet off of my own computer and have been using their's for email.  I miss everyone greatly, and really hope to hear from all of you if you are so inclined, and I promise to make my best efforts to answer in detail, though I haven't much time online, so if I am concise in my replies, please forgive me.  <br />
<br />
On a happier note, I want to thank Ziksis for volunteering for the guildleader position, as I know not too many people would want to go through the motions to truly lead.  Zik, I've heard nothing but great things, and having checked guildsay.com, I'm incredibly impressed at how you've taken the bull by the horns.  Keep up the awesome work, as I am (and will be, when I come back) proud to call you my guildleader!  <br />
<br />
So you all know, I have no desire to be leader anymore, as many of you have probably figured out already, but it truly got to be too much for me.  After awhile, the dedication and love for the guild were the only things that kept me hanging on, but my heart wasn't, and still isn't, into planning events and running around, forsaking my own needs.  As some have seen, I'm able to log on Thursday nights, and it's been great just logging on and playing.  I'm no longer dreading signing on and being expected to run around, doing things, which means I'm happier to do so when needed.  I was on last night, and had a blast fighting in DL with some of the guildies, and the only thing that was expected of me was to keep up on the haste and crack, mez, etc.  This is what EQ was about for me when I started playing, and this is what I want it to be about for me from now on.  (Of course, it goes without saying that the most important person was missing, and he would have made my time playing about 500% better than it was!)  But I'm babbling...<br />
<br />
Anyway, I implore you all to please keep in touch with me.  I miss everyone, and am grateful for the time I get to see you all once a week.  I hope to hear from you soon!<br />
<br />
All my best,<br />
Kaledine/Karuune/Dambae<br />
<br />
PS:  My email addy is Kaledine@yahoo.com						</td>
